WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.002
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 2, Network implementation, which is 20 percent of the exam.

00:00:08.002 --> 00:00:10.662
This lesson covers objective 2 point 1.

00:00:10.662 --> 00:00:13.936
Explain characteristics of routing technologies.

00:00:13.936 --> 00:00:19.870
Today's concept: BGP, and why it is the answer when routing crosses autonomous systems.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:28.810
An autonomous system, or AS, is a network under one administrative domain, such as an ISP or a company.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:36.010
Inside one autonomous system, routers use an interior gateway protocol, such as OSPF, RIP or EIGRP.

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:41.093
Between autonomous systems, routers use an exterior gateway protocol.

00:00:41.093 --> 00:00:42.330
Today that is BGP.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:44.531
BGP is a path vector protocol.

00:00:44.531 --> 00:00:49.960
Each route carries the list of autonomous systems it passes through, called the AS path.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.790
BGP peers talk over TCP port one seventy nine.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:01.937
For the exam, when routing crosses autonomous systems, the answer is BGP.

00:01:01.937 --> 00:01:06.887
It is a path vector exterior gateway protocol on TCP port one seventy nine.

00:01:06.887 --> 00:01:09.724
OSPF, RIP and EIGRP are interior protocols.

00:01:09.724 --> 00:01:11.770
That's objective two point one.
